                                    <h2>FAQs</h2>
<h3>Do I need a Bangalore-based marketing agency for my Bangalore D2C brand?</h3>
<p>Not necessarily. <strong>Category expertise matters more than location.</strong> For F&amp;B + quick-commerce-heavy brands, any agency with strong QC playbook works. For SaaS-adjacent D2C, look for content + LinkedIn + product-led growth expertise.</p>
<h3>How much does a Bangalore D2C marketing agency cost in 2026?</h3>
<p>Retainers: <strong>&#8377;1.5L&ndash;&#8377;3L/month for growth</strong>, &#8377;3L&ndash;&#8377;6L for scale. Bangalore retainers are similar to pan-India ranges.</p>
<h3>What ROAS should a Bangalore D2C brand expect?</h3>
<p>Depends on category. <strong>F&amp;B with subscription</strong>: 4&times;&ndash;6&times; (true MER 6&times;&ndash;9&times;). <strong>Healthtech</strong>: 3&times;&ndash;5&times;. <strong>Premium lifestyle</strong>: 3.5&times;&ndash;6&times;.</p>
<h3>Do you handle quick commerce (Blinkit + Zepto + Instamart)?</h3>
<p>Yes. Shelf-share strategy + paid + promotion calendar + dark-store inventory alignment. Quick commerce is 35&ndash;55% of F&amp;B category in Bangalore.</p>
<h3>Do you do SaaS marketing?</h3>
<p>Yes &mdash; content + LinkedIn + product-led growth + freemium-to-paid conversion playbooks. Different from D2C playbooks but we run both for Bangalore brands.</p>
<h3>How long is a typical Bangalore D2C engagement?</h3>
<p>Average 22 months. First 90 days is dial-in; month 4+ is scale.</p>


